upplied, so twig-grade periphery against scaffold limbs is unassessable; recorded unknown, not dismissed."], "observations": ["Only one candidate frame was supplied (render-0, B-WHOLE, in leaf); the two bare-crown/bark reference traits therefore have no matching candidate evidence channel.", "Render-0 trunk is a pale grey-white smooth column with no ridging, plating or peel; a few short dark branch stubs and faint tonal banding are the only relief.", "Crown bounding proportion in render-0 reads taller than wide, consistent with the leafed reference range.", "Interior of the render crown shows numerous light-toned limbs and sky gaps distributed to the apex; reference interior limb exposure, where present, is dark-toned and confined to the lower and mid crown.", "Trunk base sits at the lower image edge on a flat ground plane; declared framing is clipped, and no buttressed root flare is resolvable either way.", "Foliage colour in render-0 is mid to deep green with lighter outer highlights and no marked blue or grey cast, consistent with the reference foliage tone.", "Finish and style (matte surfacing, flat ground, neutral sky) sit at or above the established catalogue anchor floor; the anchor is species-irrelevant and was used for finish only.", "reference-1 and reference-2 are the same image file and checksum under two view labels, so bare-crown and bark evidence come from one frame.", "No claim is made that any reference frames depict the same specimen, and no difference between frames is attributed to change over time.", "Causes of the render's high branch union and raised skirt are not determined from the image."], "findings": [{"observation": "Render-0 carries a long slender clear bole with the first major limb division high inside the crown, whereas all reference whole-tree panels show a stout short bole breaking low into several heavy ascending scaffolds.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Could follow from a crown-base-height or first-branch parameter set above the open-grown beech range, but no mechanism is required or established."}, {"observation": "The lowest foliage in render-0 stops well clear of the ground, exposing bare trunk over a substantial fraction of tree height; references show the skirt sweeping to near ground level and shading the turf.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Consistent with the same raised-branching condition as the bole gap, but treated as a separate visible observation."}, {"observation": "Limbs in render-0 radiate steeply and near-symmetrically outward from a high union, giving a radial fan texture without stacked horizontal tiers or downward-arching tier tips.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Branch-angle distribution weighted toward ascending rather than wide-angle attachment; undetermined."}, {"observation": "Render-0 crown outline is broadly ovoid and taller than wide, matching the reference envelope, but the mass is see-through: sky and pale limbs appear throughout the upper two-thirds.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Foliage density or leaf-cluster coverage below reference level; undetermined."}, {"observation": "Trunk bark in render-0 is smooth, unfissured and mid-to-pale grey over its full visible height, matching the single strongest reference recognition cue for bark form.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Whether the render trunk bears lichen-like pale flecking cannot be determined; the bole spans too few pixels at this framing for flecks of the reference scale to register.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-2"], "impact": "required_unknown", "